BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:3rd Annual PANS/PANDAS 5K
DTSTART:20261010T100000
DTEND:20261010T120000
DTSTAMP:20261010T161636Z
UID:e6b5df1b5d36b694b2e80b861c1827@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:A 5K With a Bigger Purpose Join us on Saturday\, October 10 fo
 r the 3rd Annual Vermont PANS/PANDAS 5K Run + Walk—a joyful\, family-fri
 endly morning on the Burlington waterfront bringing our community together
  around kids and families affected by PANS/PANDAS. Race it. Walk it. Bring
  your kids. Build a team. Come as you are. Whether you’re chasing a PR o
 r taking a walk with friends\, you belong here. Expect a live DJ\, race sh
 irts\, finisher medals\, snacks\, prizes and lots of community energy\, al
 l while helping raise awareness and support for an illness too many famili
 es still struggle to have recognized. Burlington Surf Club · 50 Lakeside 
 Ave SIGN UP NOW Look what this community can do. Last year\, more than 200
  people came together to run\, walk and rally around families affected by 
 PANS/PANDAS. Together we raised more than $14\,000. This year\, we want to
  make the circle even bigger. Every registration helps build awareness. Ev
 ery person who shows up helps another family feel less alone. Why we run. 
 PANS and PANDAS can cause the sudden onset of severe behavioral\, neurolog
 ical and psychiatric symptoms in children following infection or another i
 mmune trigger. For families\, the change can be devastating\, and recognit
 ion\, diagnosis and appropriate treatment can be incredibly difficult to f
 ind. These illnesses are still far too poorly understood. We run to change
  all that. We run so more parents recognize the signs. So more teachers an
 d healthcare providers know the symptoms. So children get help sooner. And
  so families navigating PANS/PANDAS know there is a community standing bes
 ide them. Your participation makes a difference. Net proceeds from the Ver
 mont PANS/PANDAS 5K support the Neuroimmune Psychiatric Disorder Clinic at
  Dartmouth Health through our partnership with The Alex Manfull Fund\, hel
 ping advance care\, education and understanding of post-infectious neuroim
 mune disorders. A note from Gaskell family Welcome to the PANDAS/PANS 5K! 
 We are a family of 5 living in Burlington looking to transform the hardshi
 p of our own PANDAS journey into a beacon of hope and progress for others.
  In September 2022\, at age 8\, our son experienced a sudden\, acute onset
  of extreme neuropsychiatric symptoms. As his parents\, we sought help fro
 m doctors\, psychiatrists\, and local resources but to no avail\; his cond
 ition continued to spiral. Thanks to one of our son's former teachers\, wh
 o witnessed our struggle and had read about PANDAS on Facebook\, we got a 
 first glimpse of what could be happening. In June 2023\, a clinic at Dartm
 outh Hospital diagnosed our son with PANDAS. Since then\, treatment and re
 covery have been long and arduous\, however finding the right doctors\, ca
 re and support have made all the difference\, including the support of our
  community. The intense hardships of our journey have made something clear
 : we want to help others living with this devastating condition.\n\nSource
 s: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Burlington Surf Club\, 50 Lakeside Ave
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/3rd-annual
 -pans-pandas-5k-22-09-2026-10-57-12
END:VEVENT
