BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Carolan Irish Music Concert with Guitar\, Harp and More
DTSTART:20261010T140000
DTEND:20261010T160000
DTSTAMP:20261010T161636Z
UID:37c66a8b5db0295010c06f31cfe47f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:A rare celebration of the music of blind Irish harper Turlough
  O'Carolan (1670 - 1738) will feature Carolan tunes for guitar\, harp and 
 more\, in Plainfield VT on October 10 at 2 p.m. The concert\, at the Grace
  United Methodist Church and dedicated to the late musician and Carolan bi
 ographer Art Edelstein\, includes longtime Carolan musicians and will feat
 ure members of "Larks in the Attic" - a trio with Linda Young (harp)\, Pam
  Bockes (guitar) and Susan Reid (fiddle). This Celebration of the Music of
  O'Carolan marks a fresh opportunity for musicians and the public to hear 
 many of his beautiful tunes that have survived for centuries. Turlough O'C
 arolan continues to inspire harpers and Irish music lovers with his many t
 urns of mood and melody\, blending traditional styles with his own unique 
 sensibilities.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Plainfield - Grace Church\, 13 Mill Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/a-carolan-
 irish-music-concert-with-guitar-harp-and-more-16-09-2026-19-43-49
END:VEVENT
