BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cookie Queens
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261010
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261011
DTSTAMP:20261010T161636Z
UID:c3c883a03f36359a2f0e0fe602abb1@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:It’s Girl Scout cookie season and Ara\, Olive\, Nikki\, and 
 Shannon Elizabeth are vying for the coveted title bestowed to the top-sell
 ing scout: Cookie Queen. These four tenacious adolescents have big persona
 lities and big ambitions and their entrepreneurial spirit hints at bright 
 futures ahead. It isn’t just fun and games\, though\; the girls and thei
 r families make real sacrifices to hit their goals\, devoting countless ho
 urs to slinging cookies wherever and however they can. In following their 
 beats\, Cookie Queens provides a an engaging window into the $800 million 
 industry in which childhood and commerce collide. It’s a joyous\, heartw
 arming\, utterly sweet ride that cheers on the girls’ grit and ingenuity
 . Whether you’re into Thin Mints\, Samoas\, or Tagalongs\, you’ll enjo
 y this sweet and sincere celebration of girl power.\n\nSources: Vermont.co
 m\, Vermont Public
LOCATION:Main Street Landing Film House\, 60 Lake St
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/cookie-que
 ens-25-08-2026-14-07-16
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cross-Border Poetry
DTSTART:20261010T130000
DTEND:20261010T170000
DTSTAMP:20261010T161636Z
UID:f57e64faf80af0fbf9d74be0344f5f@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Sponsored by the Centre des Arts de Stanstead\, Cross-Border P
 oetry celebrates the longstanding friendship between the neighbouring comm
 unities of Canada's Eastern Townships and the state of Vermont. The aftern
 oon feature 18 poets from Vermont and Canada (including a film poem) over 
 three sessions\, with breaks in between during which people can meet the w
 riters\, enjoy refreshments\, and browse books available for purchase. The
  participating poets include Vermont Poet Laureates\, as well as winners a
 nd finalists for the Griffin Poetry Prize\, the Vermont Book Awards\, the 
 Governor General’s Literary Awards and other major honours. The beautifu
 l Haskell Opera House and Free Library embodies what is best in our region
  of the world\, and this event is a form of community pushback against div
 isive political voices at large in the world today. The event is free\, no
  registration is required\, and all are welcome.\n\nSources: Vermont Publi
 c
LOCATION:Haskell Free Library and Opera House\, 93 Caswell Avenue Derby Li
 ne\, VT 05830
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/cross-bord
 er-poetry-07-10-2026-12-46-42
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Cross-Border Poetry at the Haskell Opera House
DTSTART:20261010T130000
DTEND:20261010T170000
DTSTAMP:20261010T161636Z
UID:1ec8d9dd0180246bfe129c3088cc88@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Eighteen acclaimed poets from Canada and Vermont will gather f
 or Cross-Border Poetry on Saturday\, October 10\, 2026\, from 1:00 p.m. to
  5:00 p.m. at the historic Haskell Opera House. Sponsored by the Centre de
 s Arts de Stanstead\, this major one-day literary event will celebrate the
  longstanding friendship between the neighbouring communities of Stanstead
 \, Quebec\, and Derby Line\, Vermont. The afternoon will feature three poe
 try sessions\, with breaks offering audience members an opportunity to mee
 t the writers\, enjoy refreshments and browse books available for purchase
 . The participating poets include Vermont Poet Laureates\, as well as winn
 ers and finalists for the Griffin Poetry Prize\, the Vermont Book Award\, 
 the Governor General’s Literary Awards and other major honours. Featured
  Poets: Liz Howard\, Chard de Niord\, Katharine Whitcomb\, John Wall Barge
 r\, Kathleen Winter\, Sharon Darrow\, Jeff McRae\, Angela Leuck\, Steve Lu
 xton\, Chantal Ringuet\, Larry Bradley\, Stephanie Bolster\, Jean-Blaise B
 ourque\, Gillian Sze\, Sarah Wolfson\, Stephanie Roberts\, Jeremy Audet\, 
 and Michael Métivier. Purposefully constructed across the international b
 oundary\, the Haskell Free Library and Opera House has served the people o
 f Stanstead and Derby Line for more than a century. The border runs direct
 ly through the building\, making the Haskell an enduring symbol of coopera
 tion\, friendship and shared cultural life. The remarkable relationship be
 tween the two communities was documented in the National Film Board of Can
 ada’s 1955 film Two Countries\, One Street. In 2016\, U.S. President Bar
 ack Obama also cited the Haskell as an example of the close bonds shared b
 y Canadians and Americans. That tradition faced a challenge in 2025\, when
  long-established access through the building’s American entrance was re
 stricted for Canadian visitors. The decision followed a January visit by U
 .S. Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem\, during which\, according 
 to accounts given to CTV News\, she referred to Canada as “the 51st stat
 e” while crossing the boundary inside the building. The community respon
 ded with an extraordinary display of solidarity. A fundraising campaign wa
 s launched to create a permanent Canadian entrance\, attracting more than 
 $100\,000 in its first 48 hours. Bestselling Canadian author Louise Penny 
 contributed an additional $50\,000 to the project. The completed entrance 
 was celebrated with an official opening in June 2026. At a time when borde
 rs can be used to divide\, Cross-Border Poetry will affirm the values the 
 Haskell has embodied throughout its history: openness\, friendship\, creat
 ivity and mutual respect. The organizers invite everyone to join us for a 
 free event celebrating the values that have united us for generations. Ven
 ue: Haskell Opera House\, Derby Line\, Vermont / Stanstead\, Quebec U.S. e
 ntrance: 93 Caswell Avenue\, Derby Line\, VT 05830 Canadian entrance: 1 Ru
 e Church\, Stanstead\, QC\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Haskell Free Library and Opera House\, 93 Caswell Avenue Derby Li
 ne\, VT 05830
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/cross-bord
 er-poetry-26-08-2026-16-39-06
END:VEVENT
