DTSTAMP:20261010T161636Z
UID:69a82225a29811f023ec428f57ed1e@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Come celebrate the 3rd Anniversary of the opening of Vermont F
 orest Cemetery\, the first and currently only cemetery fully dedicated to 
 natural burial in Vermont. Join us for a day of tours\, music\, poetry\, n
 aturalism workshops\, community art and meet deathcare vendors from across
  the state. Please make sure to RSVP! Schedule of Events: 10am - 11am: Nat
 uralism Workshop led by Dirt Camp director and cemeterian Bailey McLaughli
 n. Learn about animal tracking and the natural communities of the forest. 
 11am - noon: Poetry readings in our forest labyrinth with Carlene Kucharcz
 yk\, winner of the Vermont Book Award\, in her poetry collection 'Strange 
 Hymn. In between all our events\, come meet deathcare vendors from across 
 the state: weaver Mary Lauren Fraser\, Journey with Compassion\, Camp Knoc
 k Knock\, Grief Space\, Mourning Cloak by Black Cat Atelier\, Green Mounta
 in Burial Shrouds\, Daniel Chaffee backboards and so much more! Participat
 e in a community art project and visit artist Carla Kimball's latest art i
 nstallation. We hope to see you there!\n\nSources: Vermont.com\, Vermont P
 ublic
